    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d785">

                <pb facs="0585" n="581" sameAs="frus:frus1938v04/pg581"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.512/1521: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Consul General at
                        Hankow</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Josselyn</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1938-08-06T15:00:00-04:00">August 6, 1938—3 p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>For the Ambassador. Reference Canton’s July 16, 11 a.m., in regard to transit
                    taxes. The Department assumes that you have made appropriate representations to
                    the Chinese Foreign Office.</p>
                <p>Please inform Canton that the Department has not received the despatch referred
                    to in the telegram under reference.<anchor n="25" xml:id="d785-f1"/></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d785-f1" n="25" xml:id="d785-f1-content">
                <p>The despatch (not printed) was received two days later, August 8.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
